// The residents' shops (1.4): Bea's tea room, Fern's seed counter and Tobin's pottery
// counter. Vanilla items for now: Tobin's own ware (bowls, vases, planters, tiles) needs
// its art first.
//
// Each counter carries a tile action handled by the C# mod (ArtStudio/Vale/ValeResidents.cs):
//   blinxxy.MuseArt_ValeShop <shop> <owner> <x y w h>: the shop opens when its owner stands
//   in that tile area; when they're out, the shop's ClosedMessage. When the owner isn't in
//   the world at all (the ValeResidents switch is off, or the Vale isn't open yet) it opens
//   on trust, so the stock can be tried before the residents have art.
//   blinxxy.MuseArt_ValeTeaCounter: Bea's counter, which also books her room for the night.
// The counters' tiles replace the right-click descriptions the lore branch gave Fern's and
// Tobin's counters; their ClosedMessages carry the same picture.
{
  "Changes": [
    {
      "Action": "EditData",
      "Target": "Data/Shops",
      "Entries": {
        // ---- Bea's tea room: tea, the day's food, soup in its season, cake at the weekend ----
        "blinxxy.MuseArt_ValeTeaRoom": {
          "Owners": [
            {
              "Id": "Bea",
              "Name": "BeaThistle",
